/Contents (General Science \046 Biology \055 Module 1\072 Cellular Biology and Genetics\012\0121\056 Cell Structure and Organelles\072\012The cell is the structural and functional unit of all living organisms\056 Prokaryotic cells lack a membrane\055bound nucleus\054 whereas eukaryotic cells contain defined organelles\056 Mitochondria generate adenosine triphosphate \050ATP\051 through cellular respiration\056 Ribosomes assemble amino acids into proteins following mRNA instructions\056 The endoplasmic reticulum exists in rough \050ribosome\055studded\051 and smooth forms\054 assisting in protein transport and lipid synthesis\056 Lysosomes contain digestive enzymes to break down waste materials\056\012\0122\056 Photosynthesis \046 Bioenergetics\072\012Photosynthesis converts solar light energy into chemical energy inside plant chloroplasts\056 Chlorophyll molecules absorb light in the blue and red wavelengths\054 reflecting green light\056 The light\055dependent reactions take place inside thylakoid membranes\054 splitting water molecules \050photolysis\051 to produce oxygen gas\054 ATP\054 and NADPH\056 The light\055independent Calvin cycle takes place in the stroma\054 utilizing carbon dioxide and energy molecules to synthesize glucose \050C6H12O6\051\056\012\0123\056 Molecular Genetics \046 DNA Replication\072\012DNA \050Deoxyribonucleic acid\051 stores genetic instructions in a double\055helix structure composed of nucleotides\056 Each nucleotide contains a phosphate group\054 a deoxyribose sugar\054 and one of four nitrogenous bases\072 Adenine \050A\051\054 Thymine \050T\051\054 Cytosine \050C\051\054 or Guanine \050G\051\056 Adenine bonds with Thymine via two hydrogen bonds\054 while Cytosine pairs with Guanine via three\056 During DNA replication\054 DNA helicase unwinds the double strand\054 and DNA polymerase synthesizes a complementary daughter strand in the 5\047 to 3\047 direction\056)
/DS (font\072 normal normal 9pt Helvetica\073text\055align\072left\073color\072\043000000)
