/Contents (General Science \046 Biology \055 Module 2\072 Human Systems and Ecology\012\0124\056 Human Circulatory \046 Respiratory Systems\072\012The human circulatory system operates via a closed double loop consisting of the systemic and pulmonary circuits\056 The four\055chambered heart pumps deoxygenated blood from the right ventricle into the pulmonary artery toward the lungs\056 Oxygenated blood returns via pulmonary veins to the left atrium\054 passing into the left ventricle\054 which pumps it through the aorta to body tissues\056 Red blood cells \050erythrocytes\051 utilize hemoglobin to bind oxygen\054 while white blood cells \050leukocytes\051 manage immune defenses\056\012\0125\056 Ecological Structures and Food Webs\072\012Ecosystems consist of biotic biological communities interacting with abiotic environmental factors\056 Trophic hierarchies organize energy transfer\072 Primary producers \050autotrophs\051 synthesize biomass\054 primary consumers \050herbivores\051 consume autotrophs\054 and secondary\057tertiary consumers \050carnivores\051 prey on lower levels\056 Decomposers recycle dead organic matter into nutrients\056 Only roughly 10 percent of energy transfers from one trophic level to the next\054 limiting food chain length\056)
